HOST KERNEL PATCH -- NOT applied by the Docker build. The container shares the
host's kernel, so amdkfd's device gate can only be changed in the host's
amdgpu module; build it with amdkfd-polaris10-no-pci-atomics.sh (same
directory). NOT YET RE-VERIFIED ON REAL HARDWARE.

WHY: a Polaris10 card (PCI ID 1002:67df: RX 470/480/570/580) behind a PCIe link
that cannot forward AtomicOps (typically a chipset-attached slot) never gets a
KFD node. dmesg shows:

    amdgpu 0000:05:00.0: PCIE atomic ops is not supported
    kfd kfd: skipped device 1002:67df, PCI rejects atomics 730<0

The two numbers are mec_fw_version (730, the installed MEC firmware) and
no_atomic_fw_version (0). kgd2kfd_device_init() lets a device without PCIe
atomics through only when needs_pci_atomics is false, or when a non-zero
no_atomic_fw_version is at or below mec_fw_version. kfd_device_info_init()
sets no_atomic_fw_version only for SOC15 parts (Navi1x/2x/3x, GFX11, GFX12);
the GFX7/GFX8 branch never sets it, so for Polaris10 the gate always rejects,
whatever the firmware version. Without a KFD node the card does not appear in
/sys/class/kfd, so ROCR (patched and built by this repo's Docker image) never
sees it and rocminfo lists no gfx803 agent. A card on CPU-attached lanes
(AtomicOps available) is unaffected.

WHAT: exempt CHIP_POLARIS10 from needs_pci_atomics, the same way CHIP_HAWAII is
exempted on the line above. One condition in kfd_device_info_init(). It does
not touch adev->have_atomics_support or the PCI capability, so KFD still
reports the link as having no atomics.

RISK: nothing in the kernel source establishes that Polaris10 queues, HSA
signals and SDMA behave correctly without PCIe atomics. Hawaii is exempt
because it was designed that way; Polaris10 is not. The failure mode is more
likely a silent hang or a wrong result than a clean error. Run
tools/correctness-suite and verify.py on the card before trusting it. If it
misbehaves, the fix is on the hardware side: move the card to a CPU-attached
slot.

Applies to: drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_device.c, kfd_device_info_init().
The code is identical in mainline v7.0 and master.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_device.c
@@ -245,7 +245,10 @@
 		    asic_type != CHIP_TONGA)
 			kfd->device_info.supports_cwsr = true;
 
-		if (asic_type != CHIP_HAWAII && !vf)
+		/* Same exemption as Hawaii, so the node registers on a link without PCIe AtomicOps. */
+		if (asic_type != CHIP_HAWAII &&
+		    asic_type != CHIP_POLARIS10 &&
+		    !vf)
 			kfd->device_info.needs_pci_atomics = true;
 	}
 }
